      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "5c7dee4a224821e178a26e2a5740fec4ba439ea8",
            "subject": "LU-11628 lfsck: give OST objects a missing parent FID"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 21:58:24.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 23:16:16.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20908 utils: add llapi_ost_object_migrate()",
        "message": "LU-20908 utils: add llapi_ost_object_migrate()\n\nEmptying an OST with lfs migrate rewrites every file that has an\nobject there, along with all its other objects, and lfs migrate can\nneither take a file by FID nor avoid the side effects of a group lock\non mirrored and PFL files.\n\nAdd llapi_lov_object_iterate() to walk the OST objects of a raw\nlustre.lov buffer, as fgetxattr() or llapi_scan_device() return it,\nand llapi_ost_object_migrate() to move one object to another OST with\nthe single-object layout swap.  The object is read at its own offsets\nthrough OBJECT I/O scope (LU-20802), so no stripe arithmetic is done\nhere, and copied into a one-stripe volatile file, skipping holes,\nunder a read lease that fails the move if another writer opens the\nfile; the swap checks both data versions.  LLAPI_OBJ_MIGRATE_LOCK_COPY\ntakes a group lock instead, for files that stay open for writing.\n\nThe MDS allocates the new object, as for any new object, unless the\ncaller names an OST.  The object is never put on an OST the caller\nexcludes, nor beside another copy of its data: another stripe of a\ncomponent that is not overstriped, or a mirror or parity covering the\nsame extent.  A progress callback lets the caller limit the bandwidth\nor stop the copy.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pfl\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ib1e1601e37d4051de8344345e99d9b421109faa9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
